item+ function src/seal.rs :: seal :: pub fn seal(input: &str) -> io::Result<Vec<u8>> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn seal  seals a phext: xz-compresses its full UTF-8 bytes. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 29 :: 1
item+ function src/seal.rs :: seal_bytes :: pub fn seal_bytes(input: &[u8]) -> io::Result<Vec<u8>> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn seal_bytes  seals raw phext bytes (see `seal`). ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 38 :: 1
item+ function src/seal.rs :: unseal :: pub fn unseal(data: &[u8]) -> io::Result<Vec<u8>> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn unseal  unseals a sealed phext back to its exact original bytes. Returns the io error when the data is not a valid xz stream. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 50 :: 1
item+ function src/seal.rs :: unseal_string :: pub fn unseal_string(data: &[u8]) -> io::Result<String> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn unseal_string  unseals directly to text. Fails with InvalidData when the unsealed bytes are not valid UTF-8; to unseal foreign content that may carry non-UTF-8 scrolls, `unseal` to bytes and pass them through `binary::ingest`, which applies the base64-verbatim ingestion rule instead of failing. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 65 :: 1
