item+ const src/binary.rs :: FIELD_PREFIX :: pub const FIELD_PREFIX: &str = "phext-field:base64:"; :: The prefix of a binary *field*: arbitrary bytes encoded for one line inside a text scroll (a `name=value` grammar, a WAL entry, a header block). Whole scrolls use `encode_scroll`; fields use this. :: doc comment :: 243 :: 1
item+ function src/binary.rs :: decode_field :: pub fn decode_field(text: &str) -> Option<Vec<u8>> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn decode_field  Decodes a field produced by `encode_field`. Returns None when the text lacks the field prefix or its body is not strict base64 — a plain text field is not a binary field, and yields None, not bytes. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 269 :: 1
item+ function src/binary.rs :: encode_field :: pub fn encode_field(payload: &[u8]) -> String { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn encode_field  Encodes raw bytes as a single line of text: the field prefix plus RFC 4648 base64. The result contains no line breaks and none of the nine phext dimension-break bytes, so it can sit inside any line-structured scroll. The base64 overhead (+33%) is inherent to armouring bytes in a text line; this function standardizes the armour so every implementation reads the same field the same way. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 255 :: 1
