item+ function src/phext.rs :: fetch_checked :: pub fn fetch_checked(input: &str, target: Coordinate) -> Option<String> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn fetch_checked  Fetches the scroll at `target` and returns its payload, but only when the scroll is checked and verifies. A missing, unchecked, or torn scroll yields None — recovery code can treat None as "not committed". ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1915 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: fetch_point :: pub fn fetch_point(&self, address: &str) -> String { :: ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ @fn fetch_point  fetches a point address string. A bare point is a caret: it fetches the empty string. The offset form fetches the selected characters: from the point, forward `offset` characters (scalars) within the scroll, terminating at the scroll boundary. Any parse or resolution failure fetches the empty string, as Chain::fetch does. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ :: doc comment :: 1764 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: fetch_range :: pub fn fetch_range(&self, address: &str) -> String { :: ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ @fn fetch_range  fetches a range address string: the spanned text with phext structure bytes preserved — the covered segments re-assembled at their coordinates into a phext (chain) fragment (scroll breaks between covered scrolls inside a universe, CHAIN_BREAK between universes, never a trailing CHAIN_CLOSE: a fragment is an excerpt, not a terminated chain), so the result round-trips as a phext fragment. Empty segments contribute nothing. Any parse or resolution failure fetches the empty string, as Chain::fetch does. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ :: doc comment :: 1823 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: implode :: pub fn implode(map: HashMap::<Coordinate, String>) -> String { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn implode  Serializes a hierarchical hash of scrolls into a monolithic phext document. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 963 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: is_phext_break :: pub fn is_phext_break(byte: u8) -> bool { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn is_phext_break  returns true if `byte` corresponds to one of our phext delimiters (line breaks included) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1184 :: 1
