item+ function src/phext.rs :: parse_chains :: pub fn parse_chains(input: &str) -> Vec<Chain> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn parse_chains  splits a stream into its chains. CHAIN_BREAK separates the member phexts of a chain; CHAIN_CLOSE terminates a chain, and whatever follows it opens the next one — so one stream may hold many chains. The stream's final chain is closed only when the stream ends with CHAIN_CLOSE.  Splitting follows `split_on` semantics, so empty members and empty chains are preserved exactly: parse and serialize are byte-exact inverses for every stream. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1346 :: 1
