item+ function src/phext.rs :: checked_scroll :: pub fn checked_scroll(scroll: &str) -> String { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn checked_scroll  Returns `scroll` with an integrity trailer appended: one final line `phext-check:xxh3-128:<checksum of the payload>`. In a checked scroll the final line is reserved — verification always reads the LAST marker line, and the checksum binds the entire payload before it, so a marker line inside the payload cannot forge a trailer.  The checksum detects accidental corruption and torn writes. xxh3 is not a cryptographic hash: this is integrity, not authentication. An empty scroll stays empty (a scroll with no bytes does not exist, so there is nothing to check). ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 2099 :: 1
