item+ function src/phext.rs :: parse_chains :: pub fn parse_chains(input: &str) -> Vec<Chain> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn parse_chains  splits a stream into its chains. CHAIN_BREAK separates the member phexts of a chain; CHAIN_CLOSE terminates a chain, and whatever follows it opens the next one — so one stream may hold many chains. The stream's final chain is closed only when the stream ends with CHAIN_CLOSE.  Splitting follows `split_on` semantics, so empty members and empty chains are preserved exactly: parse and serialize are byte-exact inverses for every stream. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1487 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: parse_point_address :: pub fn parse_point_address(address: &str) -> Option<PointAddress> { :: ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ @fn parse_point_address  parses a v0.6.1 point address: "[$N:]<coordinate>[@<line>,<column>[+<offsetChars>]]". Returns None on any malformed input: universe 0, a coordinate component below 1, a line or column below 1, a sign anywhere, or trailing structure. "$1:" is accepted on input; the canonical Display form never emits it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ :: doc comment :: 1876 :: 1
