item+ function src/phext.rs :: toc_children :: pub fn toc_children(input: &str, prefix: &[usize]) -> Vec<TocChild> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn toc_children  The progressive table of contents: given a coordinate prefix — the leading `prefix.len()` address components, 0 to 8 of them — returns one `TocChild` per distinct value the next dimension takes under that prefix, sorted ascending, each with the scroll count and total scroll bytes of its subtree.  A client walking a phext from the root calls `toc_children(input, &[])` for the libraries present, then `toc_children(input, &[2])` for the shelves of library 2, and so on — downloading structure one level at a time instead of the whole document. Built on the `spans` index in a single pass; scroll bodies are never copied. A prefix of 9 or more components has no next dimension and yields an empty listing, as does a prefix no scroll matches.  The children partition their parent: for any prefix shorter than 9 components, the `scrolls` of `toc_children(input, prefix)` sum to `toc_summary(input, prefix).scrolls`, and the `bytes` sum likewise.  # Example  ``` use libphext::phext::toc_children; let input = "alpha\u{17}beta\u{18}gamma"; let root = toc_children(input, &[]); assert_eq!(root.len(), 1); assert_eq!(root[0].value, 1); assert_eq!(root[0].scrolls, 3); ``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1131 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: toc_scrolls :: pub fn toc_scrolls(input: &str, prefix: &[usize]) -> Vec<TocScroll> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn toc_scrolls  Every scroll under `prefix` (0 to 9 leading address components), in document order, as a `TocScroll`: full coordinate plus byte length, no bodies. This is the planet list a progressive client renders at the bottom of a zoom — it asks for the scrolls of one star system, not of the whole phext. A full 9-component prefix yields the single scroll at that coordinate, if populated. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1176 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: toc_summary :: pub fn toc_summary(input: &str, prefix: &[usize]) -> TocSummary { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn toc_summary  The size of a subtree: the number of scrolls under `prefix` (0 to 9 leading address components) and their total byte length. `toc_summary(input, &[])` summarizes the whole document; a full 9-component prefix summarizes a single scroll — 1 scroll if it is populated, 0 if it is not. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1154 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: uncheck_scroll :: pub fn uncheck_scroll(scroll: &str) -> Option<String> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn uncheck_scroll  Returns the payload of a checked scroll when its trailer verifies; None for unchecked, malformed, or corrupted scrolls. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 2129 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: verify_checked_scroll :: pub fn verify_checked_scroll(scroll: &str) -> bool { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn verify_checked_scroll  true when `scroll` ends with a well-formed integrity trailer whose checksum matches the payload before it. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 2112 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: verify_commit :: pub fn verify_commit(input: &str, entries: &[Coordinate], commit: Coordinate) -> bool { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn verify_commit  true when the scroll at `commit` is a commit marker whose count matches `entries` and whose checksum matches the entries' current contents, in order. Any missing, altered, or torn entry — or a missing marker — yields false: the batch did not commit.  The document is indexed with a single `explode` pass and the marker and every entry are read from that map. The previous implementation ran the scanning `fetch` once for the marker and once per entry, so verification cost grew quadratically in document length — the cost a WAL recovery pass pays over the whole log, per transaction. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 2401 :: 1
item+ function src/phext.rs :: volume_break :: pub fn volume_break(&mut self) { :: ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ @fn volume_break ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ :: doc comment :: 1684 :: 1
item+ struct src/phext.rs :: Chain :: pub struct Chain { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @struct Chain  A chain: an ordered series of complete phexts within one stream, joined by CHAIN_BREAK (0x02) and optionally terminated by CHAIN_CLOSE (0x03). The chain layer is a stream-level layer, one rung above the library break: the nine dimension breaks structure a single phext, while the two chain bytes structure a stream of phexts. Each member is a whole phext, worked with the ordinary phext functions in this module; read in succession, a chain's members are editions in sequence — the chain is how a phext stream encodes time.  `closed` records how the chain ended: true when a CHAIN_CLOSE terminated it, false when the stream simply ran out (EOF). A chain that ends at EOF is unclosed — possibly truncated — and is never silently promoted to closed. A stream with no chain bytes at all is a single unclosed chain holding one member phext: every pre-0.6 phext reads this way. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1449 :: 1
item+ struct src/phext.rs :: PointAddress :: pub struct PointAddress { :: @struct PointAddress  One parsed point address: universe (1-based; 1 when the "$N:" prefix is absent), the 9D coordinate, an optional caret position, and an optional forward offset in characters. :: doc comment :: 1811 :: 1
item+ struct src/phext.rs :: RangeAddress :: pub struct RangeAddress { :: @struct RangeAddress  A parsed range: two point endpoints, normalized to ascending order at parse time. :: doc comment :: 1835 :: 1
item+ struct src/phext.rs :: ScrollPosition :: pub struct ScrollPosition { :: @struct ScrollPosition  A caret boundary inside one scroll: 1-based line and column (see the section note above). :: doc comment :: 1801 :: 1
item+ struct src/phext.rs :: TocChild :: pub struct TocChild { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @struct TocChild  One entry in a `toc_children` listing: a value taken by the next dimension below a coordinate prefix, together with the number of scrolls and the total scroll bytes in that child's subtree. Structure only — no scroll text is copied or returned. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1055 :: 1
item+ struct src/phext.rs :: TocScroll :: pub struct TocScroll { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @struct TocScroll  One entry in a `toc_scrolls` listing: a scroll's full coordinate and the byte length of its text. The planet list for progressive clients — coordinates and sizes, never bodies. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1081 :: 1
item+ struct src/phext.rs :: TocSummary :: pub struct TocSummary { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @struct TocSummary  The aggregate shape of a coordinate prefix's subtree: how many scrolls it holds and how many bytes of scroll text they carry in total. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1068 :: 1
