item+ function src/phext.rs :: toc_scrolls_by_suffix :: pub fn toc_scrolls_by_suffix(input: &str, suffix: &[usize]) -> Vec<TocScroll> { :: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- @fn toc_scrolls_by_suffix  Every scroll whose coordinate ENDS with `suffix` — the trailing 1 to 9 address components — in document order, as `TocScroll` entries (coordinate + bytes, no bodies). The relationship primitive: scrolls that share a chapter.section.scroll suffix are related wherever their library-through-book parents live, and this is the query that finds them. A 9-component suffix is a full coordinate and yields at most one scroll; an empty suffix yields every scroll, as `toc_scrolls(input, &[])` does. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- :: doc comment :: 1199 :: 1
